# Aegis judge / local demo LLM: Qwen3.5-0.8B text-only Q4_K_M (unsloth GGUF, 533 MB) with
# Ollama's built-in Qwen3.5 chat renderer/parser.
#
# Two Ollama 0.24 gotchas this works around:
#  1. `ollama pull hf.co/unsloth/Qwen3.5-0.8B-GGUF:Q4_K_M` also pulls the mmproj (vision) GGUF;
#     a model WITH a projector is routed to the bundled llama.cpp runner, which does not know the
#     `qwen35` architecture -> "unable to load model". FROM the text blob alone -> Ollama engine -> OK.
#  2. The hf.co import gets a bare "{{ .Prompt }}" template (drops system prompts, no think:false,
#     no tools). RENDERER/PARSER qwen3.5 restore the official chat format (same as library qwen3.5).
#
# download_models.sh replaces __MODEL_BLOB__ with the local blob path and runs
#   ollama create aegis-judge -f <generated Modelfile>
FROM __MODEL_BLOB__
RENDERER qwen3.5
PARSER qwen3.5
PARAMETER temperature 0.7
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER top_p 0.8
PARAMETER presence_penalty 1.5
PARAMETER num_ctx 2048
